          en: 'At the beginner level, knowing how to study means advancing faster than most contemporaries. While others accumulate dozens of courses without depth, the student with method builds a solid foundation that supports all future learning. At the junior level, this skill translates into faster onboarding in new projects and the ability to take on progressively larger responsibilities without constant supervision.\n\nAt the mid level, structured study capability allows the professional to explore new areas (infrastructure, security, performance) autonomously, expanding their scope without needing formal training in each area. In interviews, demonstrating that you know how to learn is frequently more valued than demonstrating what you already know. The technology market changes too fast for static knowledge to be sufficient. What remains relevant throughout a career is the ability to acquire new knowledge with efficiency and depth.',
