          en: '18-year-old finishing high school, no financial urgency: the most strategic recommendation is to pursue Computer Science at a good institution and, from the second year on, complement with practical projects and modern training platforms. At 22, this person will have a bachelor\'s degree, solid theoretical foundation, practical portfolio, and academic networking. It\'s the most competitive position possible for career start.\n\nPerson aged 25 or older migrating from another field: four to five years of college means entering the tech market only at 30, with high opportunity cost. The most pragmatic strategy is to start with intensive practical training to achieve employability in 6 to 12 months. Once employed, evaluate whether a degree would complement their career. Person who needs to work quickly: ADS is the shortest degree and can be combined with parallel practical training. Person targeting international market or big tech: Computer Science is nearly mandatory, as big techs list "CS degree or equivalent" as a requirement and interviews test algorithms with depth that only academic education adequately prepares for.',
