          en: 'The answer to "is college worth it?" depends entirely on who is asking, what that person wants to build, and the time horizon they are willing to consider. College without practice produces unemployed theorists. Practice without fundamentals produces executors with a growth ceiling. The most powerful combination available is solid academic foundation complemented by updated practical training and a portfolio of real projects. The most dangerous thing in this decision is not choosing the wrong path. It is having no plan at all. What makes the difference is intentionality: knowing why you are doing what you are doing, what result you expect, and how you will measure your progress.',
