          en: 'To practice, maintain a log of your searches for one week. Note what you searched, how you formulated the query, how many results you evaluated, and how long it took to find the solution. Then analyze patterns: which types of queries worked well? Which sources were most useful? Where did you lose the most time? This analysis reveals improvement opportunities that practice without reflection does not expose. Additionally, learn advanced Google search operators and explore developer-specific tools like DevDocs, which aggregates documentation from multiple technologies in a unified interface.',
